    "created_at": "2016-01-05T13:51:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-05T13:51:55Z",
    "body": "Not exactly. CDATA text is not encoded while plain text is. Whether it's an entirely distinct type or there's some meta-data describing the content, maintaining the distinction is important.\n\nThere are applications where CDATA in XML files are NOT the same as escaped string content. Round-tripping XML files in those cases would produce incorrect output.\n\nI do agree that it's not a fully distinct type, but simply losing the information would be very bad for XML processing.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
