    "created_at": "2016-01-06T14:39:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-06T14:39:33Z",
    "body": "FWIW, another data point:\nIt seems like E4X treats CDATA as content. The CDATA node when parsed in E4X is considered a normal text node, but **it includes** the CDATA tags in the text. The E4X spec is a bit vague on this point, but I do think that's the intention and that's definitely the implementation as I've observed it in ActionScript. I tried to test what the implementation was in SpiderMonkey (which is still in use in Adobe's ExtendScript), but I was having some problems getting my tests to work.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
